Script code before :CLASS: a file is a class or a script, never both
(diag.class_or_script, error, on the :CLASS token). The leading comment
is not script code; the :DECLARE is.
-- input.ssl --
/* Order helper;
:DECLARE nVersion;
:CLASS OrderHelper;
:DECLARE sOrderNo;

:PROCEDURE Describe;
	:RETURN "Order " + Me:sOrderNo;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
/* Order helper;
:DECLARE nVersion;

:CLASS OrderHelper;
:DECLARE sOrderNo;

:PROCEDURE Describe;
	:RETURN "Order " + Me:sOrderNo;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
3:1-3:7 error class_or_script: A file is either a ':CLASS' definition or a script; ':CLASS' must be the first significant statement
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
2:10-2:18 hint unused_variable: Variable 'nVersion' is declared but never used
3:1-3:7 error class_or_script: A file is either a ':CLASS' definition or a script; ':CLASS' must be the first significant statement
